# ---------------- S3: simultaneous butterfly layer ----------------
S31 = show("S3.1",
  r"With frames diagonalized by Hadamard matrices and phases $i^{\mathrm{wt}}$, the change across any edge is a product of translation kernels $C_v=aI+bX_v$, one per orthonormal basis vector of its residual, and $H_0^{\otimes D}=b^D\mathcal S_DC^{\otimes D}\mathcal S_D$.",
  r"Replace the shear frames of the bit network by phase frames $\mathcal C_U=H^{\otimes m}\operatorname{diag}(i^{q_U(x)})H^{\otimes m}$, so an edge change becomes kernels $C=H\mathsf SH=aI+bX$ on the residual directions, then return to the normalised butterfly through $H_0=b\mathsf SC\mathsf S$.",
  mot("recoverable", "Hadamard conjugation turns the diagonal phases into translations, which are exactly two-point kernels, and the residual dimension counts how many such kernels an edge needs, matching the rank count of the bit network."),
  [
   infer("S3.1.1",
     r"The complex network has total residual dimension $s_{\rm c}=W_{\rm c}m-2N+2L_{\rm c}<W_{\rm c}m$, and telescoping the phase frames gives $C^{\otimes m}$ on every role, scratch roles included.",
     Q(1218, 1224, "The sum of these basis lengths is", r"<W_{\rm c}m."), deferred=True),
   infer("S3.1.2",
     r"For an edge from label $U_-$ to $U_+$ with orthonormal residual basis $v_1,\ldots,v_{\rho_{\rm edge}}$, the frame change is $\prod_j(aI+bX_{v_j})^{\epsilon_j}$ with $\epsilon_j=\pm1$.",
     Q(1835, 1843, r"Proposition~\ref{prop:complex-motif-interface} gives the frame change", r"\epsilon_j\in\{1,-1\}.")),
   infer("S3.1.3",
     r"Applying the network with these column frames to a group of $e=mf$ axes uses exactly $s_{\rm c}$ child calls, each on the $f=e/m$ axes of one slot.",
     Q(1903, 1908, "Summing its residual dimensions gives exactly", "of one slot.")),
   infer("S3.1.4",
     r"Applying the phase identities on all selected coordinates gives $H_0^{\otimes D}=b^D\mathcal S_DC^{\otimes D}\mathcal S_D$, with exact Gaussian dyadic coefficients.",
     Q(1927, 1932, r"H_0^{\otimes D}=b^D\mathcal S_D C^{\otimes D}\mathcal S_D.")),
  ],
  page="phase-frames",
  frm=["frames", "subspace-labels", "rank-saving", "fft-butterfly", "arithmetic-modulo-2-and-linear-algebra-over-f-2", "complex-numbers", "bitwise-operations-and-xor"],
  salient="All coefficients stay Gaussian dyadics ($\\mathbb Z[i,1/2]$): the kernel $C$ has $C^2=X$ and $C^4=I$, and the plain butterfly $H_0$ is recovered from $C$ by diagonal fourth-root phases and a scalar $b^D$ that is only a shift and a phase.")

S32 = show("S3.2",
  r"Given chunks $x,y,z$ of $L=fK$ bits, the $f$ XORs $y_{j_i}\leftarrow y_{j_i}\oplus x_{j_i}$ at positions $j_i=\rho+iK$ are done by constantly many cyclic shifts of whole chunk ranges (restoring $z$) plus a deterministic repair of the exceptional addresses, a fraction at most $80(f-1)2^{-K}$, in $O(V(L^\tau+1))$ time.",
  r"Perform all $f$ XORs at once as eight packed additions that are correct whenever no $K$-bit segment lies near the edge of its field, then extract, sort and reinsert the few addresses where that fails.",
  mot("recoverable", "A shift of whole chunks costs linear time but can carry between neighbouring segments only when a segment is near the end of its range, which happens for a tiny, address-determined fraction of addresses; those can be fixed separately without depending on the payload."),
  [
   infer("S3.2.1",
     r"For a Boolean control $c$, eight conditional unit additions to integers $u,w$ flip the parity of $u$ exactly when $c=1$ and restore the auxiliary integer $w$.",
     Q(2041, 2047, "Consequently the complete output is", r"w\bigr).")),
   infer("S3.2.2",
     r"There are twenty excluded values for each of the $2(f-1)$ guards, so the exceptional set $\mathcal B$ has at most a fraction $\delta_{\rm bad}$ of the addresses, whatever the payload.",
     Q(2096, 2104, "There are exactly twenty excluded values", r"|\mathcal B|\le\delta_{\rm bad}M.")),
   infer("S3.2.3",
     r"Each rotation is a chunk swap, a controlled cyclic shift of the target chunk costing $O(V)$, and the swap undone, so the movement costs $O(V(L^\tau+1))$.",
     Q(2148, 2153, "therefore gives an $O(V)$ rotation", "rotation.")),
   infer("S3.2.4",
     r"The exceptional records are extracted with their destination ranks, stably radix-sorted and reinserted, which implements the ideal permutation $T_0$ everywhere.",
     Q(2180, 2186, "Hold the full stream untouched while", r"This implements $T_0$ everywhere.")),
   infer("S3.2.5",
     r"After division by $V$ the extra terms are $A^3/R$ and $80(f-1)2^{-K}A(1+A/R)$, which are $o(1)$ under the family bounds, leaving $O(V(L^\tau+1))$.",
     Q(2202, 2208, "After division by $V=MR$, its additional terms", r"=o(1)$.")),
  ],
  page="packed-selected-bit-addition",
  frm=["chunk-interchange", "controlled-shift", "tape-stream-operations", "bitwise-operations-and-xor", "arithmetic-modulo-2-and-linear-algebra-over-f-2", "modular-arithmetic", "finite-sets-subsets-and-counting"],
  salient="The exceptional fraction $80(f-1)2^{-K}$ is exponentially small in the chunk width $K$ and depends only on addresses, never on the record contents, so the repair is cheap in the worst case.")

S33 = show("S3.3",
  r"For $e$ active chunks one network run makes $s$ calls on slots of $e/m$ chunks, each on a stream of volume $V/W$, so the cost per unit volume satisfies $F(e)\le(s/W)F(e/m)+O((eK)^\tau+1)$, which unrolls to $O(d^{\lambda'})$ for $d$ axes with $\lambda'<1$.",
  r"Count calls per node, split the rows among the $W$ roles so every child has volume $V/W$, stop the recursion below $e<d^\beta$, and sum the geometric series of node costs over the base-$m$ pieces of the $D$ chunks.",
  mot("explicit", "The $s$ child calls run on streams of volume $V/W$, so dividing their total cost by the current volume gives the factor $s/W$.",
      Q(2409, 2413, "Indeed, the \\(s\\) child calls are executed on streams of volume", "the factor \\(s/W\\).")),
  [
   infer("S3.3.1",
     r"The phase construction supplies one recursive call on a slot for each vector in an edge residual basis, so exactly $s$ calls per invocation, and the basis changes and scalar gates at a node cost $O(V((eK)^\tau+1))$.",
     Q(2288, 2298, "The phase construction supplies one recursive call", "at this node.")),
   infer("S3.3.2",
     r"Each recursive edge call acts on one role stream with volume exactly $1/W$ of its parent's logical volume, because whole rows are sent to the $W$ roles.",
     Q(2331, 2334, "Each recursive edge call acts on", "volume.")),
   infer("S3.3.3",
     r"With $F(e)$ the time divided by the current logical volume, $F(e)\le(s/W)F(e/m)+O((eK)^\tau+1)$ and $F(e)=O(e)$ for $e<d^\beta$.",
     Q(2405, 2409, r"F(e)\le (s/W)F(e/m)+O((eK)^\tau+1)", r"F(e)=O(e)\quad(e<d^\beta).")),
   infer("S3.3.4",
     r"Adding the costs of the at most $(m-1)(1+\lfloor\log_md\rfloor)$ base-$m$ pieces and the row preprocessing gives $O(d^{\lambda'})$ for any fixed $\max\{\lambda,\sigma+\beta(1-\sigma)\}<\lambda'<1$.",
     Q(2435, 2441, "Adding their costs and the row preprocessing gives", r"=O(d^{\lambda'})")),
  ],
  frm=["recurrences-and-geometric-sums", "rank-saving"],
  salient="The same mechanism as for address chunks: each level multiplies the number of axes by $m$ but the normalised cost only by $s/W<m^\\sigma$, so the total is a power $d^{\\lambda'}$ with $\\lambda'<1$ rather than $d$.")

S34 = show("S3.4",
  r"Intermediate values in a layer on records of $r$ coefficients are exact Gaussian dyadics: reserving $p+\Delta$ fractional bits and $\Delta+3$ integer bits with $\Delta=\lceil C_0d^{C_1}\rceil=o(p)$ represents every intermediate coefficient exactly, and a single truncation $Q_p$ follows the whole contractive layer.",
  r"Bound the number of arithmetic operations on any chain through the recursion, deduce the denominator and magnitude growth from it, and reserve that many extra bits so nothing is rounded until the end.",
  mot("explicit", "The accelerated network's intermediate operators need not be contractions, so explicit constants are needed to bound denominator and magnitude growth within one layer.",
      Q(2451, 2456, "The accelerated network is evaluated exactly until", "within one layer.")),
  [
   infer("S3.4.1",
     r"The arithmetic dependency depth satisfies $A(e)\le sA(e/m)+E$ at an internal node and $A(e)\le8e$ at a leaf, so $A(e)\le8B^2d^{\nu+1}$.",
     Q(2513, 2518, r"A(e)\le sA(e/m)+E", r"at a leaf}.")),
   infer("S3.4.2",
     r"A value at depth $\ell$ lies in $2^{-(p+\ell)}\mathbb Z[i]$ and has modulus at most $2^\ell$, since addition at most doubles the modulus and halving adds one denominator bit.",
     Q(2562, 2568, r"A value at depth \(\ell\)", r"at most \(2^\ell\).")),
   infer("S3.4.3",
     r"Reserving $p+\Delta$ fractional bits and $\Delta+3$ integer and sign bits per real component represents every intermediate coefficient exactly and prevents overflow.",
     Q(2568, 2574, r"Thus reserving \(p+\Delta\) fractional bits", "prevents overflow.")),
   infer("S3.4.4",
     r"Choosing $\epsilon C_1<1$ with $d=\Theta(p^\epsilon)$ makes $\Delta=o(p)$, so the full coefficient width is still $O(p)$.",
     Q(2581, 2587, r"Choose \(\epsilon C_1<1\).", r"is \(O(p)\),")),
   infer("S3.4.5",
     r"The procedure evaluates the entire layer exactly before the final truncation $Q_p$, which changes each coefficient by less than $\sqrt2\,2^{-p}$.",
     Q(2668, 2673, r"The procedure evaluates the entire layer exactly before this final", "truncation.")),
  ],
  page="guard-bits",
  frm=["fixed-point-numbers-dyadic-rationals-and-rounding", "complex-numbers", "recurrences-and-geometric-sums", "contraction-error"])

S35 = infer("S3.5",
  r"The row construction and the recurrence analysis give total time $O(Vd^{\lambda'})$ on fixed tapes, including all padded and auxiliary streams, and the exact $C$-layer is converted to $\mathcal H$ by the phase identity.",
  Q(2736, 2740, "The row construction and the recurrence analysis", r"to $\mathcal H$."))

S36 = infer("S3.6",
  r"Every row of $\mathcal H$ has absolute row sum one, so $\mathcal H$ maps disk arrays to disk arrays, and componentwise truncation keeps the disk with error less than $\sqrt2\,2^{-p}$.",
  Q(2751, 2756, r"Finally, every row of $\mathcal H$ has", r"error less than $\sqrt2\,2^{-p}$:"))

S3 = show("S3",
  r"Applying $H_0(u,v)=((u+v)/2,(u-v)/2)$ to one selected bit in each of $D\le d$ address chunks of $K$ bits, on records of $r$ complex coefficients, costs $O(Vd^{\lambda'})$ for a fixed $\lambda'<1$, instead of $D$ whole-array passes, and is exact up to one final truncation.",
  r"Rerun the rank-saving recursion with the complex phase network: express the tensor product of $H_0$ through the kernel $C$, whose frame change on an edge is one translation kernel per residual basis vector, so each edge becomes smaller layers on slots of fewer chunks, with the binary basis changes done by packed whole-chunk moves.",
  mot("explicit", "Phase frames express a tensor product of the kernel $C$ through smaller groups of selected bits separated by binary basis changes, which are implemented by moving whole address chunks and splitting rows among the wire roles to shrink each recursive call.",
      Q(1797, 1805, "Its phase", "before one final truncation.")),
  [S31, S32, S33, S34, S35, S36],
  page="simultaneous-butterfly-layer",
  frm=["contraction-error", "fixed-point-numbers-dyadic-rationals-and-rounding", "complex-numbers", "fft-butterfly", "recurrences-and-geometric-sums", "chunk-interchange", "rank-saving"],
  salient="The cost is $O(Vd^{\\lambda'})$ for $d$ axes at once, strictly sublinear in the number of axes; it comes from the same strict inequality $s_{\\rm c}/W_{\\rm c}<m^\\sigma$ that saves a power in address interchange.",
  ad=adds(
   ("d", "chunk count", "The maximum number of address chunks whose selected bits are butterflied at once.", "count"),
   ("K", "chunk width", "The number of address bits in each chunk.", "count"),
   ("r", "record length", "The number of complex coefficients in each polynomial record.", "count")))
